prompt:
Implement a sneaker configurator using Three.js. Load MaterialsVariantsShoe.glb and support material variant switching, color adjustment, and an exploded view.

[Three.js Import Method (Must Be Followed Strictly)]
Use the following importmap in <head>, and import via ES Modules in <script type="module">:
<script type="importmap">
{ "imports": {
    "three": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/three@0.170.0/build/three.module.js",
    "three/addons/": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/three@0.170.0/examples/jsm/"
} }
</script>
<script type="module">
import * as THREE from 'three';
import { GLTFLoader } from 'three/addons/loaders/GLTFLoader.js';
import { OrbitControls } from 'three/addons/controls/OrbitControls.js';
// Write your code here
</script>

[Model Loading]
(1) Use GLTFLoader to load assets/MaterialsVariantsShoe.glb;
(2) Center the model and scale it appropriately;

[Material Variant Switching]
(3) This GLB model contains multiple material variants (Material Variants Extension);
(4) Create a button for each variant (placed in the panel with id="variantButtons");
(5) Clicking a button switches to the corresponding material variant;

[Color Adjustment]
(6) Provide a color picker (id="colorPicker", type="color");
(7) After a color is selected, apply a color tint on top of the current material (multiply it into baseColor);

[Exploded View]
(8) The "Explode" button (id="explodeBtn") moves each shoe component outward from its own center;
(9) The explosion distance is controlled by a slider (id="explodeSlider", range 0-3, step 0.1);
(10) Restore the original positions when the slider value is 0;

[OrbitControls]
(11) Support rotation and zooming for viewing;

[HUD Display]
(12) HUD in the upper-left corner:
  - Current variant name (id="currentVariant")
  - Current color hex value (id="currentColor")
  - Explosion state (id="explodeState", displaying the distance value)

[State Exposure (Required)]
Update window.__3D_STATE__ every frame:
  - modelLoaded: boolean
  - currentVariant: string
  - colorHex: string
  - explodeDistance: number
  - partCount: number (number of shoe parts)

Output a standalone HTML file.
